## Key Features of Wireless Security Testing

Professional wireless penetration testing may include Wi-Fi network discovery, access point assessments, encryption and authentication testing, rogue access point identification, guest network isolation testing, and wireless configuration reviews.

Security specialists conduct assessments within an agreed scope to minimize disruption to business operations. After testing, organizations receive a detailed report outlining identified vulnerabilities, their severity, potential business impact, and recommended remediation steps. Follow-up testing can help verify that security improvements have been implemented successfully.

